        "mat_fabrics_subheading_3": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "AURORA-TEX® LIGHT"
          }
        },
        "mat_fabrics_text_4": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The outer fabric is a special non-porous polyurethane waterproof laminate. It delivers waterproofing and breathability at a level earlier laminates couldn't reach: 20,000 mm of water resistance and 20,000 g/m²/24 hr of breathability (JIS L 1099 B-1) in a 2-layer fabric.</p>"
          }
        },
        "mat_fabrics_subheading_5": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Nylon"
          }
        },
        "mat_fabrics_text_6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>One of the lighter synthetic fibers, with high tensile and abrasion strength. It's smooth, resists wrinkles, and releases dirt easily, so it's easy to care for. It absorbs little moisture and dries quickly when wet, and it bonds well with water-repellent and waterproof-breathable coatings.</p><p><em>Denier (D) measures the thickness of a synthetic yarn: a 1-denier yarn 9,000 m (about 5.6 miles) long weighs 1 g. The higher the denier, the thicker the yarn, and fabric woven from thicker yarn is stronger.</em></p>"
          }
        }
